[size=5][b]Eternia Co-op[/b][/size]
Play battles with up to 4 players, like the PS1 original. Each controller controls its own party member.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Open the game folder: Steam → right-click Tales of Eternia Remastered → Manage → Browse local files.
[*]Extract the zip into that folder (BepInEx is included).
[*]Start the game. You'll see "Eternia Co-op" in the top-right of the title screen.
[/list]

[size=4][b]How to play[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Plug in controllers - player 2 gets the 2nd character, player 3 the 3rd, and so on.
[*]Players 2–4 control their character in battle. Menus and the field stay with player 1, like the PS1.
[*]Press [b]F1[/b] (or hold [b]L3 + R3[/b] on a controller) to choose who is which player.
[*]To let the AI play a character again, set it to [b]Auto[/b] in the Skills menu.
[*]Playing online? Use [b]Parsec[/b] - only the host needs the mod.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Up to 4 players in battle
[*]Automatic controller setup - join or leave mid-battle
[*]Controller manager (F1 / L3 + R3)
[*]Semi-Auto / Auto tab for every character
[*]Each player's controller rumbles for their own character
[/list]

[size=4][b]Safe to use[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]No internet access, tracking or telemetry
[*]Doesn't change any game files - delete it and the game is back to normal
[*]Turns itself off if a game update changes things
[*]Open source on [url=https://github.com/thewhitejesus/EterniaCoop]GitHub[/url]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tested with 2 players. 3–4 players and Parsec should work - feedback welcome!
[*]Using [b]Guests from Phantasia[/b]? It also uses L3 + R3. Set [i]ManagerControllerShortcut = LB+RB+Back[/i] in [i]BepInEx\config\eterniacoop.cfg[/i].
[*]A controller shows up twice? Turn off Steam Input for the game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [i]winhttp.dll[/i], [i]doorstop_config.ini[/i], [i].doorstop_version[/i], [i]changelog.txt[/i], [i]EterniaCoop-README.md[/i] and the [i]BepInEx[/i] folder.

[size=4][b]Permissions[/b][/size]
Free to share, modify and reupload (MIT license) - just keep the credits.

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
Created by thewhitejesus1 with Claude (Anthropic). Uses BepInEx, HarmonyX, UnityDoorstop and MonoMod. Inspired by EusthEnoptEron's arise-multiplayer.
